diagnosis_text:
No active fault found. We validated inter-room reachability from multiple Office LAN (192.168.3.0/24) hosts and all paths are working as expected. From office_pc (192.168.3.2), ICMP to the Server Room host pc1 (1.0.0.5) and Internet Lab hosts pc3/pc4 (128.168.0.3/0.4) succeeds with 0% loss and ~1–2 ms RTT. Independently, enquiry, exam_cell, and tpo also reach both pc1 and pc3 with 0% loss. This demonstrates that L3 routing via router1 (Office uplink) across the inter-router links to router2 (Servers/Internet Lab) is healthy, and there is no isolation of the Office VLAN.

Mechanism: The reported “timeouts beyond our room” are not reproducible; successful cross-subnet pings indicate forwarding, ARP/ND, and routing tables are operating normally. Localization: Office LAN via switch2 -> router1 -> WAN r1–r2 -> router2 -> target VLANs all pass traffic.

Root cause: No ongoing network misconfiguration or outage detected; the earlier issue was likely transient or host-specific and has cleared.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Recommend closing the ticket and monitoring. If symptoms recur, capture traceroute and timestamps from an affected Office host, and try renewing the host’s IP/ARP (ip addr renew/flush or DHCP renew) to speed local recovery. === END ===